{
  // PvE-specific corrections only - objective patches plus the few task-level
  // fields that genuinely differ in PvE (`taskRequirements`, `disabled`).
  // Anything true of every mode belongs in src/overrides/tasks.json5, even when
  // the supporting capture came from PvE.

  // Building Foundations - the PvE client roots this task at A Helping Hand,
  // while regular and pvp-season upstream require Swift Retribution (complete
  // or failed). The shared override had been forcing the PvE edge into every
  // mode, which made the task appear available in PvP once A Helping Hand was
  // done. The PvP report and the wiki's Requirements section both place the
  // task behind Swift Retribution / Inevitable Response, so only PvE keeps the
  // A Helping Hand edge.
  // Proof: https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/Building_Foundations
  //        https://github.com/tarkovtracker-org/tarkov-data-overlay/issues/384
  //        https://github.com/tarkovtracker-org/tarkov-data-overlay/issues/356
  '673f629c5b555b53460cf827': {
    taskRequirements: [
      {
        task: { id: '6752f6d83038f7df520c83e8', name: 'A Helping Hand' },
        status: ['complete'],
      }, // Was (shared/API): Swift Retribution, complete or failed
    ],
  },

  // Pathfinder's old PvE-only objective text is gone: the 1.1 client has no
  // extract-7-times objective left.
  // Was: Survive and extract on Interchange 7 times
  // All three AvailableForFinish conditions are VisitPlace counters
  // (shorl_exit_ne, shorl_exit_se, shorl_exit_pp) that match the upstream
  // "Visit the ... exit" objectives in every mode, so the override was removed
  // rather than corrected.
  // Proof: https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/Pathfinder
  //        https://github.com/tarkovtracker-org/tarkov-data-overlay/issues/387

  // Small Business - Part 3 - the two Woods objective texts are swapped relative
  // to their actual map markers. The game data's zone IDs/positions are correct;
  // this swaps only the descriptions so each names the marked location.
  // Proof: https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/Small_Business_-_Part_3
  '66631493312343839d032d22': {
    objectives: {
      '666733e565831d5bafa18bbb': {
        description: 'Stash a Cultist knife at the sawmill marked circle on Woods', // Was: river village
      },
      '666733e7430c8972d6a5f438': {
        description: 'Stash a Cultist knife at the river village marked circle on Woods', // Was: sawmill
      },
    },
  },

  // Collector - PvE uses a different Chemical prerequisite than regular.
  // Proof: https://github.com/tarkovtracker-org/tarkov-data-overlay/issues/356
  //
  // The 1.1-pve capture's Quest start condition targets Chemical - Part 4
  // (597a0f5686f774273b74f676) and accepts status [4, 5] = complete or failed.
  // The 2026-08-27 regular capture instead targets Chemical - Part 3 accepting
  // complete only, and the wiki Requirements section agrees with regular - so
  // Chemical - Part 3 is the shared value in src/overrides/tasks.json5 and this
  // PvE-only entry restores the PvE edge. The other three edges are identical in
  // both captures and stay shared.
  '5c51aac186f77432ea65c552': {
    taskRequirements: [
      {
        task: { id: '597a0f5686f774273b74f676', name: 'Chemical - Part 4' },
        status: ['complete', 'failed'],
      }, // Was (shared/API): Chemical - Part 3, complete only
      {
        task: { id: '5c0bde0986f77479cf22c2f8', name: 'Shooter Born in Heaven' },
        status: ['complete'],
      },
      {
        task: { id: '5bc480a686f7741af0342e29', name: 'The Tarkov Shooter - Part 4' },
        status: ['complete'],
      },
      {
        task: { id: '5ae4497b86f7744cf402ed00', name: 'Sew it Good - Part 2' },
        status: ['complete'],
      },
    ],
  },

  // New Beginning - prestige track, and PvE has no prestige.
  // Proof: https://github.com/tarkovtracker-org/tarkov-data-overlay/issues/362
  //        https://github.com/tarkovtracker-org/tarkov-data-overlay/issues/319
  //        https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/New_Beginning_(Prestige_1)
  //
  // This task is not an ordinary trader quest: it is the Quest start condition
  // on prestige element 672df12f97f0469cea52f55e (Prestige 1), returned by
  // `client/prestige/list`. Upstream itself agrees PvE has no prestige -
  // `json.tarkov.dev/pve/tasks` serves `prestige: []` while
  // `json.tarkov.dev/regular/tasks` serves all six prestige elements - yet it
  // still lists the quest whose only purpose is to gate Prestige 1. The local
  // captures agree: no PvE session is served `client/prestige/list`, and this
  // repository already scopes every prestige correction to
  // src/overrides/modes/regular/prestige.json5.
  //
  // Two independent reporters at levels 35 and 36 (both above the wiki's level-25
  // requirement) confirm the quest never appears in PvE.
  //
  // Note the PvE capture is build 1.1.0.1.46699 rather than the 46911 used for
  // the other modes, so the endpoint evidence alone would carry a version
  // caveat; the empty upstream `prestige` array for PvE is what removes it.
  '6761f28a022f60bb320f3e95': {
    disabled: true, // Was: active (pve has no prestige track)
  },
}
